;;; sha256sum_shani_x86.shard — THE SHA-NI VARIANT BIN's machine+weld
;;; article (Arc B rung B5, E3 slice C — docs/STREAM.md §8.4; landed
;;; from e3c_probe 2026-08-09). sha256sum_stream_x86.shard's twin at
;;; the world-VECTOR grain (xvrun_w/wveval), over the variant module.
;;;
;;; THE MODULE (vfm_m shape, spelled open in every walk claim): the
;;; skeleton's fifteen slots with TWO deltas — fn 1 = snw_wrap (the
;;; fused SHA-NI fold leaf, sha256.snweld.shard; the scalar fold
;;; caller's exact boundary) and fn 13 = vfm_init (the init wrapper
;;; EXTENDED per the ratified endianness lean):
;;;   XCall 14 (gb_shinit_x: writes K BE + H BE at 130752/131008),
;;;   then the 16 mask bytes at 130496 (XStore8 immediates — the
;;;   pshufb byte-flip constant), then K -> LE (mask into XMM1, 16 x
;;;   [vload group; XVBswap32; vstore] at 130752+16i; K is
;;;   fold-private — only fn 1 reads it), then the XMM-file
;;;   ground-zero (16 vloads from the dead-zero cell 130512) for
;;;   LOOP-HEAD UNIFORMITY, then RDI := 0. The H window is NOT
;;;   touched: it stays BIG-endian at every boundary the
;;;   absorber/finalizer see — fn 7 (hex) reads its BYTES at 131008.
;;;
;;; Body fns vfm_copy/abs/fin/loop/read/write/exit are byte-copies of
;;; the skeleton's sfm_/ssm_ bodies ((inline F) is same-file-only);
;;; the vfm_*_tie claims at the end of this file pin them to the
;;; skeleton article's originals so cross-file drift fails AT THE TIE.
;;;
;;; The tiers, bottom to top (records = STREAM.md §8.4 slice-C
;;; bullets): the init-walk twin (vin_wcall at S^587 c; vim_* mask/
;;; K-conversion folds + the vki_mem consumers), the callee ladders
;;; (vtr/vtw/vcp/vfp/vhx: each landed sweld walk cert lifted through
;;; xvcall_bridge then wvcall_bridge with the XMM lanes riding), the
;;; absorber/finalizer twins (vsm_abs/fin_wseq/wcall; fold site =
;;; snw_wcall, sst_xabsorb/xfinal value haves transplanted verbatim),
;;; ground-fuel packagings + shim mirrors + iteration pieces + the
;;; 18-cell VECTOR INVARIANT (vsm_vstep_thru) + walks + the machine
;;; entry equations vsm_main_eof/err/dry at xvrun_w fn 9 (S^1390),
;;; and THE WELD TIER (vsw_): the readback twins over the
;;; hbsw∘fmem∘hbsw sandwich (K observation DROPPED — the variant K
;;; window is LE and fold-private; the package plugs (sha_k)), the
;;; step/invariant twins, and vsw_main_eof — THE SEALED DONE LEG:
;;; from all-zero registers, ANY XMM file, a zero total cell, and
;;; the zero cell at 130512, for EVERY oracle behavior at every
;;; sufficient fuel the bin writes bytes_hex (sha256 (scat chunks))
;;; and exits 0. Ground validation was e3c_run.shard (init + init->
;;; fold composition differential, 7/7).

